"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with a design phase, followed by a development phase led by Omar Jensen. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule and the addition of team members Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. A $2M budget was approved by the executive board. The project is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November, with UI enhancements planned for October. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, will be updated in January. Additionally, the team is exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology integration."
